    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:49b18e3fb3f9ec7b",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "0ce6e123cc19a08a605f27bac25d92ab81d89c31667d2ff80a04b01603872119",
      "text": "Day 12 · Breakfast and flight to Trujillo. Your guide meets you at the airport for a tour beginning at Chan Chan, capital of the Chimú kingdom and the largest adobe city of the pre-Columbian Americas. Continue to the seaside town of Huanchaco, famous for its fishermen and their traditional reed boats, the caballitos de totora, which have ridden the Pacific waves for generations. Visit the majestic Temples of the Sun and the Moon, built by the Moche civilisation, whose striking murals and mythological symbols reveal ancient beliefs, and the Huacas de la Fertilidad, associated with fertility cults. Time for lunch between visits; in the evening, comfortable bus to Chiclayo and transfer to the hotel.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "word_exact",
        "fileId": "1mZ4jhPLYLzUFjyOH1D1pe9UINgA601dT",
